  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Centrale des Syndicats des Travailleurs du Rwanda (CESTRAR) and the Congr&#xe9;s du Travail et de la Fraternet&#xe9; au Rwanda (COTRAF) and their affiliated sectoral federations, adopted a three-year time-bound action plan (2022-2025) on the ratification and application of International Labour Standards in June 2022. The action plan entails trade union membership organizing, recruitment, retention, union renewal, employment and productivity improvement, social dialogue, bi- and tripartism, skills development, school-to-work transition and entrepreneurship, social protection, minimum wage, labour migration, child labour, equality and non-discrimination, the future of work, training, research and networking.  As a result, CESTRAR and COTRAF have maintained a coherent approach to respond to social and economic situations; ensuring the inclusion and involvement of all categories of workers in trade union decision-making structures, women, youth, workers with disability.  Other categories include migrant workers, and workers in the informal economy. Furthermore, the two confederations have contributed to the development of policies (no 66/2018 of 30/08/2018) regulating labour in Rwanda, extending its scope to cover both formal and informal workers that not only recognize, but also respect the rights of women, youth, and workers in the informal economy. It also includes their rights to freedom of association and collective bargaining as well as social protection. This is in line with the Rwanda DWCP, UN Development Assistant Plan (UNDAP) and Vision 2050. CESTRAR has held nationwide talk shows on TV and Radio to advocate for the ratification of Conventions nos. 88, 97, 131, 143, 189, 190, and Protocol no. 29. The ILO provide support to two workshops for the CESTRAR and COTRAF on the themes &quot;Planning time-bound actions to inform the organized labour&apos;s agenda and effective service delivery for increased trade union membership&#x201d; in June 2022, and &#x201c;Role of trade unions in extending social protection coverage to workers in the informal economy and other marginalized groups in Rwanda&#x201d; in March 2023. 

In addition, ILO provided technical assistance that informed CESTRAR&apos;s constructive participation in the UN High-level Political Forum in New York in July 2023.

As a result of a joint initiative, the Centrale des Syndicats des Travailleurs du Rwanda (CESTRAR) and the Congr&#xe9;s du Travail et de la Fraternet&#xe9; au Rwanda (COTRAF) identified existing social protection gaps and determined priorities that informed the development and adoption of a trade unions&apos; roadmap for advocating and influencing national policies, strategies, and for closing the identified gaps.</narrative>
   </description>
